{"document":1,"title":"user in #8550ddae:answer_c8354ae9: I'm planning a summer dinner party and want to cre...","updated_at":"2023-05-22T08:52:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"That's a lot of great ideas! I'm particularly interested in the Lavender Dream, as I've been experimenting with lavender in my cocktails lately. Speaking of which, I tried a lavender gin fizz recipe last weekend, but it didn't quite turn out as expected - I didn't have simple syrup, so I had to improvise with honey and water. Do you have any tips on making a good simple syrup, or would you recommend a specific brand?","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"8550ddae:answer_c8354ae9\"}"}
{"document":1,"title":"user in #8550ddae:answer_c8354ae9: I'm planning a summer dinner party and want to cre...","updated_at":"2023-05-22T08:52:00+00:00","source_type":"slack","content":"If you prefer to buy simple syrup, there are many excellent brands available. Here are a few popular ones: 1. **Monin:** A well-known brand in the bartender community, Monin offers a range of flavored simple syrups, including a classic 1:1 simple syrup. 2. **Finest Call:** Another popular brand, Finest Call offers a simple syrup made with pure cane sugar and filtered water. 3. **Small Hand Foods:** This artisanal brand offers a range of flavorful simple syrups, including a classic 1:1 and a honey-based syrup. For your Lavender Dream cocktail, you can use either a homemade or store-bought simple syrup. If you're using honey, keep in mind that it will add a distinct flavor profile to your cocktail. Now, let's get back to your Lavender Dream! How did you infuse your gin with lavender, and what ratio of gin to lavender did you use? I'd be happy to help you refine the recipe.\nThanks for the tips on making simple syrup! I think I'll try making my own this weekend. For the Lavender Dream, I actually didn't infuse my gin with lavender, I just found a recipe online that called for lavender syrup and gin. I didn't have lavender syrup, so I tried to make a lavender gin fizz instead, but like I said, it didn't turn out so well. Anyway, I was thinking of experimenting with different gin brands for my summer dinner party. Can you recommend any good ones?","metadata":"{\"Channel\": \"8550ddae:answer_c8354ae9\"}"}
